a7fdd1f4af22334421328735971275cae30d0316e301412dc1cd859" "q-115256/selection/77d9af67304d92a0ab5557c9669415c9523b236e0304adeec18c70e3187f5c30"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115256" :question/id #uuid "bbb96456-68ae-5b30-9f53-6b93317d471e" :question/math-academy-id "q-115256" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{6})\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any even function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ is symmetric across the $y$-axis, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{6})$ is an even function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡((-x)^{6}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{6}) \\\\  & =f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{6})$ is an even function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{6})\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{6})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115256/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2688742c-1655-557a-888d-af7e2179a89c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115256"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-88206"] :question/problem "${\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any even function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ is symmetric across the $y$-axis, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)$ is an even function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5(-x)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-5x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x) \\\\  & =f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)$ is an even function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-88585/selection/620027d1afdbb394ef64b860e490de7b079b0be021911f6ff5b691e9d05e3189" :answer/id #uuid "3baddf13-f0b6-5ace-9873-99dc05236d87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88585/selection/8c5b341640c01b6836731d1e34e362a3691c51b85dc74f639633cb19aacdaa28" :answer/id #uuid "9a4e5687-aa81-58b3-aa6c-3b379ddfe892" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88585/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "26faacf8-1d22-5b0d-8a19-66e6dba74e06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88585/selection/a20cd085f197379821972957e859918d110e8909dab55fcd85c4ccdabdf198c3" :answer/id #uuid "b526c854-3d10-5f5e-9ef9-67e95870a066" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88585/selection/08bdee2885d9d77f0a17de94004a6ed7068919e4c1e70e8f1a0768e555094af8" :answer/id #uuid "f216eece-2660-5e20-9d7a-870c2f0e3afe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88585/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "abb72f35-3021-589c-bada-e1dd8e941a1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-88585/selection/08bdee2885d9d77f0a17de94004a6ed7068919e4c1e70e8f1a0768e555094af8" :answer-field/choices ["q-88585/selection/620027d1afdbb394ef64b860e490de7b079b0be021911f6ff5b691e9d05e3189" "q-88585/selection/8c5b341640c01b6836731d1e34e362a3691c51b85dc74f639633cb19aacdaa28" "q-88585/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-88585/selection/a20cd085f197379821972957e859918d110e8909dab55fcd85c4ccdabdf198c3" "q-88585/selection/08bdee2885d9d77f0a17de94004a6ed7068919e4c1e70e8f1a0768e555094af8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-88585" :question/id #uuid "1e5fda12-e16b-50c6-8bc6-86826ee8106a" :question/math-academy-id "q-88585" :question/problem "Simplify the integral ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x$ using symmetry." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any even function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ is symmetric across the $y$-axis, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{4})$ is an even function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =3\\operatorname{tan}⁡((-x)^{4}) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{4}) \\\\  & =f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{4})$ is an even function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{1}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-88585/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2688742c-1655-557a-888d-af7e2179a89c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-88585"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-88582/selection/503c